{"from": "claim:lk-05-catching-people", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-04-18-fishermen-called", "note": "Same call of Simon as Matthew 4:18-22, but Luke sets it after a miraculous catch of fish, not while casting nets; Luke names no Andrew."}
{"from": "claim:lk-05-left-everything", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-04-18-fishermen-called", "note": "Matthew has the fishermen leave their nets and boat; Luke has them leave 'everything' after the catch."}
{"from": "claim:lk-05-roof-tiles", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-02-04-roof-dug-through", "note": "Luke says the carriers let him down 'through the tiles' (dia ton keramon); Mark says they dug through/uncovered the roof; Matthew 9:2 does not describe the roof."}
{"from": "claim:lk-05-levi-called", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-09-matthew-tax-office", "note": "Luke names the tax collector Levi, not Matthew; Mark names Levi son of Alphaeus; the traditional identification with Matthew the apostle is not made by Luke."}
{"from": "claim:lk-05-levi-called", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-02-14-levi-alphaeus-tax-office", "note": "Luke names Levi but omits 'son of Alphaeus'."}
{"from": "claim:lk-05-physician-sinners", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-13-mercy-not-sacrifice", "note": "Luke keeps the physician saying and 'sinners to repentance' but omits Matthew 9:13's quotation of Hosea 6:6, 'I desire mercy, and not sacrifice'."}
