{"from": "text:josephus-war-3-gennesaret", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-05-gennesaret-lake", "grade": "B", "note": "Josephus: 'This lake is called by the people of the country the Lake of Gennesareth' - the lake by the same local name in the period (the naming itself is attested grade A on place:sea-of-galilee); it confirms the setting, not the crowd."}
{"from": "artifact:galilee-boat", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-05-washing-nets", "grade": "C", "note": "A 1st-century fishing boat recovered in 1986 on the north-west shore: boats stood by this working lake; context, not the scene (no evidence connects the boat to Jesus or his disciples)."}
{"from": "artifact:magdala-fishing-gear", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-05-washing-nets", "grade": "C", "note": "A needle and lead weights for repairing and holding down fishing nets from the 1970s Magdala excavations - the net washing and repair the verse describes, as excavated equipment."}
{"from": "artifact:galilee-boat", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-05-taught-from-boat", "grade": "C", "note": "The excavated boat is 8.2 m long - a platform from which a teacher could address a crowd on shore; context for the scene, not the event."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-3-gennesaret", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-05-washing-nets", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus on the lake: 'There are several kinds of fish in it, different both to the taste and the sight from those elsewhere' - the rich fishery the nets assume; context, not the catch."}
